WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.850
Chapter 07 lists the dangers to the
evidence, and the guard for each.

2
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:09.063
A record edited after closure would
say something the re-read didn't,

3
00:00:09.063 --> 00:00:13.200
so the export recomputes the evidence
hash and reports a mismatch.

4
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.605
Evidence cut short by the
field length can't be parsed,

5
00:00:16.605 --> 00:00:20.088
so it's reported, and the
attachment holds the full copy.

6
00:00:20.088 --> 00:00:25.537
A close that bypassed the business rule is
named: closed without re-read evidence.

7
00:00:25.537 --> 00:00:29.489
A record deleted from the period
would make the package look complete,

8
00:00:29.489 --> 00:00:32.213
but the chain breaks and
the verifier reports it.

9
00:00:32.213 --> 00:00:36.565
Fields filled in to look complete would
claim an approval that never happened,

10
00:00:36.565 --> 00:00:40.249
so later-pass fields stay null with
their reason, and tests pin that.

11
00:00:40.249 --> 00:00:44.500
And if the export ran with the verifier's
role, it could close findings,

12
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:48.960
so it runs under its own read-only role,
which the kit's call list can check.
